{"name":"Fern","hex":"#548d44","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name.","A topographic surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern","wikidata":"Q80005"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Equisetopsida.jpg/500px-Equisetopsida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Equisetopsida.jpg/500px-Equisetopsida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEquisetopsida.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Flickr_-_brewbooks_-_Angiopteris_evecta_-_Mule%27s_foot_fern_%281%29.jpg/500px-Flickr_-_brewbooks_-_Angiopteris_evecta_-_Mule%27s_foot_fern_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Flickr_-_brewbooks_-_Angiopteris_evecta_-_Mule%27s_foot_fern_%281%29.jpg/1280px-Flickr_-_brewbooks_-_Angiopteris_evecta_-_Mule%27s_foot_fern_%281%29.jpg